@prefix this: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix sub: <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/> .
@prefix np: <http://www.nanopub.org/nschema#> .
@prefix npx: <http://purl.org/nanopub/x/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix delphi: <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/> .

sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/blueprint-well-formedness> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "An emitted anatomical blueprint graph is well-formed under its own rules (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "A finite graph of ontology terms with a body root, levels and part_of edges is well-formed when every edge goes strictly down in level, every edge joins two nodes, every non-root node has a whole, and the pinned taxon statements exclude nothing: then part_of is acyclic, its closure is transitive, every node reaches the root, and a Boolean checker whose truth implies all of this can be evaluated by the kernel on each emitted blueprint." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean) for the organism thread's text-to-blueprint tool; structural well-formedness, no paper states it." ;
    skos:notation "LevelsDown ∧ Closed ∧ (∀ a ≠ root, ∃ b, a part_of b) ⟹ Acyclic ∧ Rooted ; check g D = true ⟹ WellFormed g D" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **Soundness of the checker.** If `check g D` evaluates to `true`, the graph is well-formed. -/
theorem wellFormed_of_check (g : Graph α) (D : TaxonData α τ) (h : check g D = true) : WellFormed g D"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Blueprint.Graph" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Blueprint.wellFormed_of_check", "Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.acyclic_of_levelsDown", "Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.transGen_trans", "Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.transGen_level_lt", "Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.rooted_of" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Structural only. The certificate says the emitted structure is internally coherent under its stated rules; it does not say the organism is real, that the anatomy is correct or complete, that Uberon or the Cell Ontology are right, or anything about a transition between forms." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/blueprint-well-formedness> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/blueprint-well-formedness> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-blueprint-well-formedness> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-blueprint-well-formedness> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Blueprint.wellFormed_of_check with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 3 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean (198 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Blueprint.wellFormed_of_check, Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.acyclic_of_levelsDown, Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.transGen_trans, Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.transGen_level_lt, Delphi.Blueprint.Graph.rooted_of: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 3 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [blueprint-certificate-cycle] Data sabotaged: an edge making the body root part of node 1 is added to the certified edge list (an upward edge, closing a cycle through the root). The kernel-evaluated checker must reject it. Rejected with 2 error(s): AFlyingFish.lean:30:76: error: Tactic `decide` proved that the proposition [blueprint-certificate-excluded-taxon] Data sabotaged: a never_in_taxon row saying node 1 is never in Vertebrata (NCBITaxon 7742, an ancestor of Exocoetidae) is added. The checker must reject it. Rejected with 1 error(s): AFlyingFish.lean:30:76: error: (kernel) application type mismatch [blueprint-closure-level-flipped] Statement changed to claim the level INCREASES along the part_of closure (level a < level b) instead of decreasing; acyclicity rests on this lemma, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 2 error(s): Blueprint.lean:83:31: error: Application type mismatch: The argument Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/blueprint-well-formedness> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

sub:provenance {
  sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Blueprint.lean> , <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json> , <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci lean thread (Claude Fable 5.1 writing the Lean modules and this builder; the Lean kernel, not the model, checked the proofs)" ;
    delphi:usesModel <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a delphi:LanguageModel ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1" ;
    dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" .
}

sub:pubinfo {
  this: dct:created "2026-10-31T22:03:26.216Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    dct:creator <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> ;
    rdfs:comment "Owner ORCID not yet set: the key owner passes --owner <orcid> to lean/nanopubs/build.mjs at signing time; until then no human is named in this record." ;
    rdfs:label "An emitted anatomical blueprint graph is well-formed under its own rules: machine-checked in Lean 4" ;
    dct:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    npx:hasNanopubType <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Concept> ;
    rdfs:comment "Hand-authored in Delphi ontology v2.0 terms (https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/) by the builder, not created from a template. The template that would otherwise apply as Provenance template is <https://w3id.org/np/RAaYeFYF-Cz2bM5S1wPQsnvs5X6BBxsphL03UkbVZ1lcA>. Its published copy carries no legacy probknow IRI (checked 2026-10-31); it was consulted but not instantiated, so no template is declared. A template-conformance checker will therefore report no template declared." ;
    rdfs:comment "Hand-authored in Delphi ontology v2.0 terms (https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/) by the builder, not created from a template. The template that would otherwise apply as Pubinfo template is <https://w3id.org/np/RAtKj9bCnB4gUe0E9k-WhffQFSEWd9Ve2hrVllYoLuOB0>. Its published copy still uses legacy w3id.org/probknow IRIs (2 occurrences when checked on 2026-10-31), and its required statements cannot be instantiated from v2.0 terms, so it was not used and no template is declared. A template-conformance checker will therefore report no template declared." ;
    npx:introduces <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/blueprint-well-formedness> ;
    delphi:domain <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/math-population-genetics-and-evolutionary-theory> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/domain/math-population-genetics-and-evolutionary-theory> rdfs:label "math-population-genetics-and-evolutionary-theory" .
}
